    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d750">

                <pb facs="0700" n="688" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg688"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.51A/4: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Moose</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-20T13:00:00+03:06">April 20, 1944—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:49 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>116. Department’s 65, April 18, 9 p.m. It would be of interest to know substance
                    of London’s 3073 April 15, noon, which was not repeated here.<anchor n="82"
                        xml:id="d750-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Telling King that, if he so desires President is ready to name military adviser
                    might be useful. If King desires, adviser designation of officer becomes detail;
                    if not, refusal might set a useful precedent should question again arise.</p>
                <pb facs="0701" n="689" xml:id="pg689"/>
                <p>In my opinion subject of financial adviser should not now be discussed other than
                    to say that if King would like Americans in advisory capacity Government would
                    give sympathetic consideration to any request. Specific proposal for financial
                    adviser might be considered when plans for increased financial aid to Saudi
                    Arabia take more definite shape.</p>
                <p>Colonel Eddy will accompany me to Riyadh and no objection is perceived if he
                    wishes to remain there or to return a second time. He is willing to accept post
                    as military adviser.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moose</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
